    "result_text": "The acceptance suite is the complete test suite. All green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature so that owners in the same household share a stable identifier.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` field to the `Owner` response schema (this drives the generated `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct auto-maps).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `householdId` field mapped to a `household_id` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` + `schema.sql`, so this is required).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Reworked the household logic:\n   - Computes the set of existing owners in the same household (same normalized last name + address).\n   - When `sharesHousehold` is `true`: assigns the owner a shared `householdId` \u2014 reusing an existing member's id if present, otherwise deriving a stable one, and backfilling any household members that lack it.\n   - When `false`: keeps the existing behavior of rejecting a duplicate household with `409 CONFLICT`.\n   - Added a `householdId(Owner)` helper that derives a deterministic `HH-<12 hex>` identifier from the normalized last name + address (SHA-256), so every member of a household independently derives the same stable value.\n\n**Design note:** I made `householdId` a deterministic function of the household key (last name + address). This guarantees all members share the identical value (satisfying the test's `hb == hc` assertion) and makes it genuinely \"stable\" \u2014 it's the same across restarts and independent of creation order \u2014 while still backfilling existing records to honor \"assign both the same householdId.\"\n\n**Tests:** Full suite green \u2014 `Tests run: 21, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (including the new `Cp11Tests` and the existing `Cp10Tests` household-duplicate rules).",
